# License — the texts

The transcriptions served by The Neoplatonic Library are transcriptions of
printed works that are in the **public domain**. Everything printed in the
source editions was published before 1929 and its copyright has expired; no
copyright is claimed over the transcribed words, over the scans they were read
from, or over the plain transcriptions served here.

This covers:

- `data/editions/*/versions/*/source.txt` — the served transcriptions, byte
  copies of scans of the public-domain prints;
- the text served at `/texts/<slug>/`, `/texts/<slug>/v/<semver>/` and the
  `/v/<semver>/plain` exports.

You may copy, quote, redistribute and reuse the transcribed texts for any
purpose, including commercial use, without asking and without attribution. A
citation is still the scholarly thing to do, and each edition page prints one.

## What is NOT public domain here

- **The editorial layer** — the repairs, the page models, the apparatus, the
  notes, the graph, the site's own prose — is original work and is licensed
  separately under CC-BY-4.0; see `LICENSE-editorial`.
- **The build tooling** (`build/`, `tools/`, `elm/`) is licensed under the MIT
  license, the same split the blog uses.
- The **scans** the transcriptions were read from belong to the institutions
  that hold the physical copies (Archive.org items named per edition in
  `scan_source`); their terms are theirs and are linked on each edition page.
